## Why This Is Asked

Tests knowledge of production-grade model serving, stateful components, and zero-downtime updates under streaming data.

## Key Concepts

- Embedding sharding and stateful serving
- Online updates without stale reads
- Atomic model version swaps and canary deployment
- Observability, SLAs, rollback strategies

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code: versioned embedding cache lookup
const version = process.env.MODEL_VERSION || 'v1';
const embedCache = loadEmbeddingCache(version);

function predict(inputIds) {
  const emb = embedCache.lookup(inputIds);
  return model.apply(emb);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test zero-downtime swap guarantees?
- What race conditions could arise and how would you mitigate them?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests real-world streaming inference design, per-model batching, and robust rollout strategies in TF Serving, including stateful handling for ASR and safe upgrades.

## Key Concepts
- Streaming inference for ASR
- Per-model dynamic batching and isolation
- Stateful routing per session
- Canary rollouts with latency/throughput targets

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example: pseudo streaming buffer
function feedChunk(sessionId, chunk) {
  if (!state[sessionId]) state[sessionId] = [];
  state[sessionId].push(chunk);
  if (state[sessionId].length >= 4) {
    // call inference for the buffered chunks
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate tail latency under burst traffic?
- How would you detect and respond to model drift in streaming inputs?
- How would you extend this to add a third modality (text) with routing?
